meta {
  name: Campaign Reclassify (confirm)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/internal/campaign-reclassify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  x-internal-secret: {{internalServiceSecret}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "meta_campaign_id": "23851234567890123",
    "campaign_type_id": "{{campaignTypeId}}",
    "dry_run": false,
    "actor_id": "{{userId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  The real fan-out, in one transaction:

  RELABEL is unconditional -- every branch's campaign row and every lead on it
  gets the corrected type.

  RE-ROUTE is deliberately narrow. A lead only changes hands if it is still
  auto-assigned and untouched by a person, sits in an open stage, has ZERO
  interactions, AND its current owner holds no weight for the new type in that
  branch. Each is re-picked in ITS OWN branch's rotation; an empty target pool
  leaves it unassigned with a logged reason, never back on the old pool.

  A lead someone has already called keeps its owner and only its label is
  corrected. That is a product decision, not a heuristic.

  actor_id is optional and stamps lead_assignment_log.assigned_by_id so the
  move is attributable on the lead timeline.

  Returns { dry_run, campaigns_relabelled, leads_relabelled, leads_reassigned,
  leads_left_unassigned, by_branch[] }.
}
